 "title": "Research Themes | IIM Bangalore",
 "text": "Research Themes\nBusiness Strategies and Challenges in Indian IT services and software product organizations\nVarious aspects of software engineering management and project management in global IT and software organizations\nOutsourcing of knowledge-intensive services\nGlobally distributed work\nHuman Resource Management in IT and ITES organizations\nIT in Economic Development\nKnowledge Management in Indian software and IT organizations\nInnovation and Competition in IT industry\nGovernance in the Indian IT sector\nContemporary IT based learning systems\nE-Governance\nQuality of products, processes and services in the Indian IT industry\nMetrics and data generation on Indian IT industry\nStudy / Consultation Reports\nPal, Abhipsa, Dattathrani, Sai and De', R. ‘User-Level Security Issues in Mobile Payments’, 2017.\nDattathrani, Sai and De', R. 'Open-source vendor evaluation framework', 2016.\nDattathrani, Sai. 'Market Research Consultation Report for Agricultural Supply Chain Performance Monitoring Tool', 2016.\nResearch Papers From CSITM\nRao, R.A. and De', R. ‘Open-Source Reuse and Strategic Imperatives’, in Sim, S.E. and Gallardo-Valencia, R.E. (eds) Finding Source Code on the Web for Remix and Reuse, Springer, pp. 187-204, 2013.\nPrakash and De (2007) ‘Importance of development context in ICT4D projects: A study of computerization of land records in India’, Emerald Insight/ Information Technology & People/vol20 issue 3\nMahadevan, B. and Srinivasan, G. (2003). ‘Software for manufacturing cell formation: Issues and Experiences’, GT/CM World Symposium. July 28-30, 2003, Columbus, OH.\nProf. N.M. Agrawal (2001) - Creating Organizational Culture for Knowledge Management, IIMB Review\nProf. N.M. Agrawal and Prof. M.R. Rao (2002) - Developing Human Capital for Sustaining Growth of Indian IT Industry, AHRD Conference Book\nProf. N.M. Agrawal and Mohan Thite (2003) - Human resource issues: challenges and strategies in the Indian software industry, International Journal of Human Resource Management and Development\nProf. N.M. Agrawal and Prof. Mohan Thite (2006) - Nature and Importance of Soft Skills in Software Project Leaders, Asia Pacific Management Review (2006) 11(2), 405-413\nProf. N.M. Agrawal, Prof. Naresh Khatri and Prof. R. Srinivasan (2011) - Managing growth: Human resource management challenges facing the Indian software industry, Journal of World Business Volume 47, Issue 2, April 2012, Pages 159-166\nProf. N.M. Agrawal, Rajesh Pandit and Divya Menon (2012) - Strategy to usher in the next phase of growth in the Indian IT industry, IIMB Management Review Volume 24, Issue 3, September 2012, Pages 164-179\nProf. N.M. Agrawal, Prof. M.R. Rao and Sudheesh Venkatesh (2014) - Education and Employability: Learning from the Indian IT /ITES Industry, Book Chapter in the book published by Cologne University, Germany\nProf. N.M. Agrawal, Prof. Dhara Shah and Prof. Mirriam Moeller (2020) - Career decisions of married Indian IT female expatriates, Journal of Global Mobility Vol. 7 No. 4, 2019, Pages: 395-418\nProf. N.M. Agrawal, Pratyush Bharati, Kui Du, Abhijit Chaudhury (2021) - Idea Co-creation on Social Media Platforms: Towards a Theory of Social Ideation, The Data Base for Advances in Information Systems\nCompleted Research Projects\nProf Shankar Venkatgiri: Openworld - A study of open-source e-learning environments that can be integrated to enhance the learning portal at IIMB and make it replicable.\nProf Raghunath: Boundary Spanners and Client Vendor Relationships in IT Outsourcing: A Social Capital Perspective Social Media, Big Data and Innovation Business Models and Strategies for Cloud Computing\nMarket Research consultation report for Agricultural Supply Chain Performance Monitoring Tool. A final report on tool recommendation along with market outlook was submitted in September 2016\nResearch on open-source vendor evaluation to create a framework for evaluation of open-source vendors in India (completed in 2016-17)\nSecurity in Mobile Payments: A Report on User Issues to focus on risks associated with Indian mobile phone-based payment systems (completed in 2016-17)\nChanging nature of Alliances and Partnerships with the changing IT business models (completed in 2016-17)\nWorking Papers\nRamesh G; L S Murty (2011) Working paper of IIMB titled Determinants of Management Control at Responsibility Centre Level : Software Industry as a Case. D. V. R. Seshadri, James A. Narus (2004), Offshore Outsourcing of High Tech Jobs: The View from India\nProf. N.M. Agrawal (1998) - Managing Knowledge Workers: Benchmarking Indian IT Organization",
